  "update_count": 56,
  "description_snippet": "VULNERABILITY DETAILS\r\nSpecially crafted JavaScript can cause Chrome to use an instance of any class as if it was an instance of pretty much any other class. This allows an \"arbitrary bad cast\": an attacker can call almost any method of almost any class `A` on an object of almost any other class `B`"
